                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10950300-a988-36d5-87f6-1a5d4c990b94",
                        "entry_id": "7dfb6ca3-526a-3426-92d2-080c01fabac8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Krankheit, (a) in Kombination mit dem Namen des Erstbeschreibers oder (b) als Beschreibung eines singulären Krankheitsbildes wie beispielsweise Morbus haemolyticus neonatorum"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "38528229-6e4a-4794-b996-2ee618265ef8",
                                "sense_id": "10950300-a988-36d5-87f6-1a5d4c990b94",
                                "text": "Der Schauspieler leidet seit einiger Zeit an Morbus Parkinson."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7cfb64e-6477-47ff-a3b4-74976ce9d8ec",
                        "source_entry_id": "7dfb6ca3-526a-3426-92d2-080c01fabac8",
                        "source_sense_id": "10950300-a988-36d5-87f6-1a5d4c990b94",
                        "source_sense_description": "Krankheit",
                        "target_lang_word": "disease",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disease",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7c7c695-5e2d-335f-b345-d3073fda4c46",
                                        "entry_id": "35e18628-d3ac-3a20-87e5-8a3f3e7c98b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An abnormal condition of a human, animal or plant that causes discomfort or dysfunction; distinct from injury insofar as the latter is usually instantaneously acquired."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65e527e5-feca-4bf3-887e-f42daff3833a",
                                                "sense_id": "f7c7c695-5e2d-335f-b345-d3073fda4c46",
                                                "text": "The tomato plants had some kind of disease that left their leaves splotchy and fruit withered."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06978ee3-50e1-4607-973d-abc486fd6b48",
                                                "sense_id": "f7c7c695-5e2d-335f-b345-d3073fda4c46",
                                                "text": "[…] diſeaſes deſperate growne,\n By deſperate appliance are releeued,\n Or not at all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff849cfc-b28e-4cc8-8096-941f71e527d2",
                                                "sense_id": "f7c7c695-5e2d-335f-b345-d3073fda4c46",
                                                "text": "The instability, injustice, and confusion, introduced into the public councils, have, in truth, been the mortal diseases under which popular governments have every where perished; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8e5a240-18a1-496f-a243-de0f16566357",
                                                "sense_id": "f7c7c695-5e2d-335f-b345-d3073fda4c46",
                                                "text": "Of all the queer collections of humans outside of a crazy asylum, it seemed to me this sanitarium was the cup winner. […] When you're well enough off so's you don't have to fret about anything but your heft or your diseases you begin to get queer, I suppose."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4943e791-f785-4d0e-a21c-e19e198b1b1e",
                                                "sense_id": "f7c7c695-5e2d-335f-b345-d3073fda4c46",
                                                "text": "[…] the awfully hearty sort of Christmas cards that people do send to other people that they don't know at all well. You know. The kind that have mottoes […] And then, when you see [the senders], you probably find that they are the most melancholy old folk with malignant diseases."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c62834e-ac46-4331-af8d-82cb5fc927c9",
                                                "sense_id": "f7c7c695-5e2d-335f-b345-d3073fda4c46",
                                                "text": "Conditions were horrendous aboard most British naval vessels at the time. Scurvy and other diseases ran rampant, killing more seamen each year than all other causes combined, including combat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9bc328d-c8bb-3435-98d8-72ba55264bd9",
                                        "entry_id": "35e18628-d3ac-3a20-87e5-8a3f3e7c98b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any abnormal or harmful condition, as of society, people's attitudes, way of living etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d84af51e-0af2-447a-8e80-56678a50337f",
                                                "sense_id": "b9bc328d-c8bb-3435-98d8-72ba55264bd9",
                                                "text": "War is not man's great and terrible disease; war is a symptom, a result. The real disease is the virus of national sovereignty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00976ac3-e880-3a3d-bc5c-697b3691f81a",
                                        "entry_id": "35e18628-d3ac-3a20-87e5-8a3f3e7c98b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lack of ease; uneasiness; trouble; vexation; disquiet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "298910fb-1d40-42a6-9f6d-f328025c29ff",
                                                "sense_id": "00976ac3-e880-3a3d-bc5c-697b3691f81a",
                                                "text": "To ſhield thee from diſeaſes of the world, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disease",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c88de7b-4225-397a-8032-4923b8ccd57a",
                                        "entry_id": "a4d4992e-a6eb-3a6e-b459-876592e54d5d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause unease; to annoy, irritate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3fb4ae7-5f3c-427a-891b-daafb76a4a7a",
                                                "sense_id": "8c88de7b-4225-397a-8032-4923b8ccd57a",
                                                "text": "Whyll he yett ſpeake\n there cam won from the rulers off the ſynagogis houſſe\n which ſayde to hym: Thy doughter is deed\n diſeaſe not the maſter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45417c54-088f-4f58-875a-f93073f8884f",
                                                "sense_id": "8c88de7b-4225-397a-8032-4923b8ccd57a",
                                                "text": "[…]mote he ſoft himſelfe appeaſe,\n And fairely fare on foot, how euer loth;\n His double burden did him ſore diſeaſe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57fe137c-1782-327d-810a-bb0e9b980c6c",
                                        "entry_id": "a4d4992e-a6eb-3a6e-b459-876592e54d5d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To infect with a disease."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "45b07b3b-4b8d-465e-a447-b8fa4fd239b6",
                        "source_entry_id": "7dfb6ca3-526a-3426-92d2-080c01fabac8",
                        "source_sense_id": "10950300-a988-36d5-87f6-1a5d4c990b94",
                        "source_sense_description": "Krankheit",
                        "target_lang_word": "maladie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "maladie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1261d192-c5a8-3dfb-83ac-2c30d694fcf3",
                                        "entry_id": "c2a443e5-1f4e-3c04-b25b-2c93ae7ec176",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Problème de santé chez un être vivant qui se traduit par une baisse des capacités physiques ou par un dysfonctionnement, une altération du métabolisme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "addf9745-8f2d-45d3-bee8-4924c4371f28",
                                                "sense_id": "1261d192-c5a8-3dfb-83ac-2c30d694fcf3",
                                                "text": "De toutes les maladies, la plus sauvage, c'est de mépriser notre être."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32d11200-1d4f-4bb3-9704-606b0d658846",
                                                "sense_id": "1261d192-c5a8-3dfb-83ac-2c30d694fcf3",
                                                "text": "[…] je ne voulais pas me faire à l’idée que mon père fût mort, et que plus jamais il ne reviendrait. Durant sa maladie, on m’avait défendu de pénétrer dans sa chambre, et il était parti sans que je l’eusse embrassé."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1723cfb8-2d36-4408-95e6-4c935621d00e",
                                                "sense_id": "1261d192-c5a8-3dfb-83ac-2c30d694fcf3",
                                                "text": "On dit des bêtes, à la campagne, qu’« elles ont la maladie », sans préciser laquelle. Henri avait « la maladie »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d1051fa-124d-466b-a005-797917e31ad2",
                                                "sense_id": "1261d192-c5a8-3dfb-83ac-2c30d694fcf3",
                                                "text": "Après Prévost, il faudra attendre près de 50 ans encore et traverser les terribles famines d’Irlande pour que l'on reconnaisse enfin de façon irréfutable que les champignons vivants peuvent être la cause de maladies chez les végétaux."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d521a9b8-a120-43d3-8a37-13652863cf1f",
                                                "sense_id": "1261d192-c5a8-3dfb-83ac-2c30d694fcf3",
                                                "text": "Pasteur diagnostiqua le mal : c’était la maladie dite des morts flats ou flacherie, indépendante de la pébrine. Contrairement à l’opinion générale, deux maladies différentes, mais concomitantes, décimaient les magnaneries."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73154479-7594-3634-bab4-c9d75a2decb8",
                                        "entry_id": "c2a443e5-1f4e-3c04-b25b-2c93ae7ec176",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(Précédé de l'article défini) Menstruations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "euphemism",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "373271ca-8ecb-4a96-b9b3-3f007423c726",
                                                "sense_id": "73154479-7594-3634-bab4-c9d75a2decb8",
                                                "text": "Une maladie est tout processus qui porte atteinte aux fonctions normales d’un animal. Toutefois, si un individu dont un membre est fracturé peut, en principe et dans la mesure où il ne peut plus se mouvoir correctement, être considéré comme souffrant d’une maladie, il reste que, dans la pratique, ce terme exclut en général les dysfonctionnements d’origine accidentelle. Les maladies se divisent en plusieurs types […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c809a280-5b31-4a6b-bcaa-8cb28efc35f1",
                                                "sense_id": "73154479-7594-3634-bab4-c9d75a2decb8",
                                                "text": "Ce mois-ci, donc, j'attendais la maladie vers le 10 juin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d022e66-2c87-384e-b0b9-0fec8840509c",
                                        "entry_id": "c2a443e5-1f4e-3c04-b25b-2c93ae7ec176",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mal moral."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edbfeaea-4511-4597-b1c6-85570dea278d",
                                                "sense_id": "0d022e66-2c87-384e-b0b9-0fec8840509c",
                                                "text": "On se souvient que le pape avait décrit 15 maladies à Noël en 2014, lors de son adresse au haut clergé de la curie vaticane. Le cardinal Wuerls ne serait-il pas atteint de la maladie 14, celle des cercles fermés? En effet, il a fait carrière comme évêque de Pittsburgh de 1988 à 2006, puis archevêque de Washington. Vivait-il dans un genre de bulle ecclésiastique?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79aec813-90f9-3416-a50f-0bcf3de355c0",
                                        "entry_id": "c2a443e5-1f4e-3c04-b25b-2c93ae7ec176",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Affection excessive pour quelque chose ; manie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d48a962-c298-44b2-b1e7-57dc967b1011",
                                                "sense_id": "79aec813-90f9-3416-a50f-0bcf3de355c0",
                                                "text": "Rome a eu l’équivalent des purges et procès à grand spectacle, et de la maladie du soupçon ; tout sénateur était soupçonnable, et il en fut ainsi jusqu'à la fin de l'Empire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "baa89420-fd68-42b7-b5a5-ad1ecaddf340",
                                                "sense_id": "79aec813-90f9-3416-a50f-0bcf3de355c0",
                                                "text": "Tu regardes tous les jours ce vieux feuilleton ? C’est une vraie maladie !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
